    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0375" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg305"/>

                <head>No. 161.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Denaut.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 6,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your note of
                    the 3d instant, transmitting copies of the proceedings of the second session of
                    the international conference for the protection of submarine cables, and
                    expressing the hope that the project may not be amended by this Government, but
                    that full powers may be given to the American delegates to sign the treaty, I
                    have to inform you that this Government has no desire to hamper the conclusion
                    of the treaty by any suggestions or amendments, but is prepared to sign it on
                    the day fixed.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
